  "label": "the overallintent",
  "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts a Black surgeon in scrubs, surgical cap, and mask, with text overlay reading 'when you've finished with your life of crime.' This juxtaposition maps the image of a medical professional onto the metaphor of a 'life of crime,' implying that the person's profession is somehow connected to criminal behavior. This is a harmful stereotype rooted in anti-Black racism, specifically the long-standing and damaging trope that associates Black people with criminality. The meme uses the visual of a respected professional to ironically or cynically suggest that their career is somehow 'criminal' or morally suspect, which can be interpreted as a form of racial stereotyping and can contribute to the marginalization of Black professionals in medicine. The intent is to provoke a reaction through the juxtaposition of a respected profession with a derogatory stereotype, potentially reinforcing harmful biases.",
